===============================================
1. OVERVIEW
===============================================

The UDART Intelligent Maintenance Management System is a comprehensive
fleet maintenance platform designed to manage the University of Dar es
Salaam transport fleet. Built with Laravel 11 and modern web
technologies, it unifies drivers, technicians, storekeepers, supervisors,
and administrators on one platform — replacing paper records and
phone-call workflows with a structured, real-time system.

MISSION STATEMENT
-----------------
To provide a reliable, intelligent, and role-aware platform that
maximises bus uptime through structured repair workflows, proactive
preventive maintenance, real-time IoT health monitoring, and AI-driven
failure prediction.

===============================================
2. FEATURES
===============================================

FLEET MANAGEMENT
----------------
- Real-Time Fleet Board — live view of every bus split into On the Road,
  At the Depot, In Maintenance, and Unavailable groups
- 10 Bus Statuses — granular tracking from active through on_trip,
  under_repair, awaiting_spare_parts, ready_for_service, and more
- Maintenance Lock — overdue-PM buses are automatically locked from dispatch
- Mileage Logging — per-trip odometer tracking that feeds into PM
  interval calculations

WORK ORDER WORKFLOW
-------------------
- 10-Stage Pipeline — Reported > Pending > Assessment > Pending Approval >
  Assigned > (Awaiting Parts / In Progress) > Testing > Completed >
  Returned to Service
- Priority Levels — Low, Medium, High, Critical with visual badges
- Spare Part Linking — record parts consumed per work order; stock
  deducted automatically
- Status Audit Trail — every transition is time-stamped and attributed
  to the acting user

PREVENTIVE MAINTENANCE
----------------------
- 10 Service Templates — Oil Change, Brake Inspection, Tyre Rotation,
  Air Filter, Battery, Coolant, Transmission, Full Inspection,
  Wheel Alignment, Wiper Blades
- Intelligent Interval Scoring — 0-120 point algorithm adjusts intervals
  for high-risk vehicles (Critical buses serviced at 50% of standard
  interval)
- Auto-Generate All — one click creates PM schedules for every bus x
  every service type
- Automatic Enforcement — daily scheduler marks overdue PM, sends 7-day
  and 3-day warnings, and locks non-compliant buses

SPARE PARTS INVENTORY
---------------------
- Full CRUD Catalogue — part number, quantity, minimum stock, unit
  price, supplier
- Low-Stock Alerts — broadcast notification fires automatically when
  stock hits minimum
- Usage History — every part tracks which work orders consumed how
  many units

IOT SENSOR MONITORING
---------------------
- ESP32 Integration — microcontrollers on each bus push readings via
  HTTPS API
- 4 Sensor Parameters — Engine Temperature, Vibration, Oil Pressure,
  Battery Voltage
- 3-Level Health Classification — Normal / Warning / Critical with
  instant alerts
- Time-Series Charts — per-bus sensor history visualised on the IoT
  dashboard

AI FAILURE PREDICTION
---------------------
- Flask ML Microservice — separate Python service analyses features and
  returns predictions
- 8-Feature Input — mileage, days since service, 30-day sensor averages,
  failure history
- Risk Levels — Low / Medium / High with confidence score and recommended
  action
- Bulk or Per-Bus — run predictions for one bus or the entire active
  fleet at once

FAILURE PATTERN ANALYSIS
------------------------
- Top Failure Types — most frequent fault descriptions fleet-wide
- High-Risk Buses — vehicles with 3+ failures in the last 90 days
- 12-Month Trend — bar chart showing whether fleet health is improving
- Per-Bus Drill-Down — recurring fault types with occurrence count and
  average interval

MULTI-ROLE ACCESS
-----------------
- 5 Distinct Roles — Administrator, Supervisor, Technician,
  Storekeeper, Driver
- 29 Fine-Grained Permissions — individual permission grants/revocations
  per user
- Role-Based Dashboards — every role sees a different dashboard tailored
  to their job
- OTP Account Activation — email OTP flow ensures only legitimate staff
  activate accounts

NOTIFICATIONS & MESSAGING
--------------------------
- In-App Notification Centre — personal and broadcast alerts with
  read/unread tracking
- 14 Trigger Events — PM overdue, sensor critical, WO assigned, bus
  locked, low stock, and more
- Thread-Based Messaging — internal communication with 4 categories
  (General, Protocol, Urgent, Maintenance)

REPORTS & EXPORTS
-----------------
- 3 Report Types — Maintenance, Inventory, Fleet Performance
- 3 Export Formats — PDF, CSV, Excel (XLSX)
- Interactive Charts — Chart.js bar and pie charts in every report
- MTTR Calculation — Mean Time To Repair computed per bus

===============================================
3. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
===============================================

TECHNOLOGY STACK
----------------

  Layer                   Technology
  ----------------------  ------------------------------------------
  Backend Framework       Laravel 11 (PHP 8.2+)
  Frontend                Bootstrap 5, Blade Templates, Chart.js
  Database                MySQL 8.0+
  Authentication & RBAC   Laravel Breeze + Spatie/Laravel-Permission
  IoT Endpoint            RESTful API (ESP32 over HTTPS)
  ML / AI Service         Flask (Python) — separate microservice
  PDF Export              DomPDF
  Excel/CSV Export        Maatwebsite/Excel
  Email                   Laravel Mail (SMTP) — OTP delivery
  Localisation            English & Swahili
  Scheduling              Laravel Artisan Task Scheduler

DATABASE SCHEMA
---------------

  users                        All staff accounts
  roles                        5 predefined roles
  permissions                  29 individual permissions
  model_has_roles              User <> Role mapping
  model_has_permissions        Per-user permission overrides
  role_has_permissions         Default permissions per role
  buses                        Fleet vehicle records
  work_orders                  Repair tasks with full status history
  maintenance_records          Completed maintenance logs
  preventive_maintenance       PM schedules (1 row per bus per service)
  spare_parts                  Inventory catalogue
  spare_part_usages            Parts consumed per work order
  sensor_readings              Raw IoT data from ESP32 devices
  failure_predictions          AI model output per bus
  notifications                Personal and broadcast alerts
  daily_bus_assignments        Morning dispatch records
  mileage_logs                 Per-trip odometer entries
  message_threads              Internal messaging threads
  messages                     Individual thread messages
  message_thread_participants  Thread membership + read receipts

===============================================
4. PREREQUISITES
===============================================

SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS
-------------------
  - PHP 8.2 or higher
  - MySQL 8.0+
  - Web Server: Apache 2.4+ or Nginx 1.18+
  - Node.js 18+ (for asset compilation)
  - Composer 2.0+

EXTERNAL SERVICES
-----------------
  - SMTP Server        for OTP email delivery to new users
  - Flask ML Service   Python service for AI failure predictions (optional)
  - ESP32 IoT Devices  microcontrollers fitted on each bus (optional)

===============================================
5. INSTALLATION
===============================================

Step 1 — Clone the Repository
------------------------------
  git clone <repository-url> udart
  cd udart

Step 2 — Install Dependencies
-------------------------------
  composer install
  npm install && npm run build

Step 3 — Environment Configuration
------------------------------------
  cp .env.example .env
  php artisan key:generate

Step 4 — Database Setup
-------------------------
  mysql -u root -p -e "CREATE DATABASE udart_db;"
  php artisan migrate --seed

Step 5 — Start Development Server
-----------------------------------
  php artisan serve

  In a separate terminal (enables PM scheduling and notifications):
  php artisan schedule:work

  Optional — start the Flask ML service for AI predictions:
  cd ml-service
  pip install -r requirements.txt
  python app.py

Open http://localhost:8000 in your browser and log in with any of
the default accounts listed in Section 11.

===============================================
6. CONFIGURATION
===============================================

DATABASE
--------
  DB_CONNECTION=mysql
  DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
  DB_PORT=3306
  DB_DATABASE=udart_db
  DB_USERNAME=your_username
  DB_PASSWORD=your_password

EMAIL (OTP DELIVERY)
---------------------
  MAIL_MAILER=smtp
  MAIL_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
  MAIL_PORT=587
  MAIL_USERNAME=noreply@udart.co.tz
  MAIL_PASSWORD=your-app-password
  MAIL_ENCRYPTION=tls
  MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=noreply@udart.co.tz
  MAIL_FROM_NAME="UDART System"

IOT DEVICE AUTHENTICATION
--------------------------
  ESP32_SECRET=your-shared-secret-token

AI PREDICTION SERVICE (FLASK)
------------------------------
  FLASK_ML_URL=http://localhost:5000

PORTFOLIO DEMO MODE
-------------------
  DEMO_MODE=true

  Guests visiting / see a project overview page. With DEMO_MODE=true the
  overview and sign-in pages also list one seeded account per role
  (see config/demo.php) with a quick-fill button. Sign-in still goes
  through the normal login, OTP check and role permissions.

  Only enable DEMO_MODE on a database populated by the demo seeder, which
  loads the sample data (dates relative to today) plus today's dispatch,
  with the demo driver guaranteed a bus:
    php artisan migrate:fresh --seed --seeder=DemoSeeder

  For a public demo also set APP_ENV=production, APP_DEBUG=false,
  MAIL_MAILER=log (so no OTP emails are sent), a fresh APP_KEY and a new
  ESP32_SECRET, and re-run the command above on a schedule (e.g. nightly,
  after midnight) so visitor changes are reset.

===============================================
7. USAGE
===============================================

7.1 GETTING STARTED
--------------------
  1. Access the system at http://localhost:8000
  2. Log in with an admin account (see Section 11)
  3. Explore the fleet board at /fleet-board for a live picture of the fleet
  4. Create bus records under /buses before adding any other data
  5. Run auto-generate at /preventive-maintenance to create PM schedules
  6. Assign drivers to buses each morning via /bus-assignments

-----------------------------------------------
7.2 USER ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES
-----------------------------------------------

ADMINISTRATOR — Full System Access
  - Creates and manages all user accounts; assigns roles; overrides
    individual permissions
  - Registers new buses, updates bus details, and decommissions vehicles
  - Creates and advances work orders through the full repair pipeline
  - Manages preventive maintenance schedules and triggers auto-generate
  - Manages spare-parts catalogue — adds parts, sets minimum stock levels
  - Runs AI failure predictions for any bus or the entire fleet
  - Views IoT sensor dashboard and per-bus sensor history
  - Generates and exports all report types
  - Manages role permissions globally

SUPERVISOR — Operations Management
  - Registers buses and updates bus records
  - Creates work orders for reported faults; advances status through
    assessment > approval > assignment > return-to-service
  - Creates and manages preventive maintenance schedules
  - Records spare parts used in repairs (auto-deducted from stock)
  - Manages daily dispatch — assigns buses to drivers each morning
  - Views fleet board, IoT sensors, and AI predictions
  - Generates and exports all reports

TECHNICIAN — Workshop Floor
  - Views work orders assigned to them on their personalised dashboard
  - Advances work order status as the repair progresses
    (In Progress > Testing > Completed)
  - Logs completed maintenance work in maintenance records
    (description, cost, parts replaced)
  - Views spare parts to check stock availability
  - Views IoT sensor readings and AI predictions for a bus before
    starting work

STOREKEEPER — Inventory Management
  - Adds new parts to the catalogue (part number, quantity, minimum
    stock, price, supplier)
  - Updates stock quantities after receiving deliveries
  - Views critically low parts highlighted in red on their dashboard
  - Views part usage history to understand consumption patterns
  - Generates and exports the inventory report

DRIVER — Field Operations
  - Views today's bus assignment from a simplified, separate portal
  - Starts a trip — changes bus status to on_trip
  - Ends a trip — logs km travelled, odometer reading, and route
  - Reports breakdowns directly — creates a work order instantly and
    alerts maintenance
  - Tracks repair progress on all breakdown reports they have submitted

-----------------------------------------------
7.3 DAY-TO-DAY SYSTEM FLOW
-----------------------------------------------

  MORNING DISPATCH
  Supervisor > /bus-assignments > assigns bus to driver > driver notified

  TRIP START
  Driver > /driver/dashboard > Start Trip > bus status: on_trip

  BREAKDOWN OCCURS
  Driver > Report Breakdown > work order created (status: reported)
                            > bus status: breakdown_reported
                            > all maintenance staff notified (broadcast)

  REPAIR WORKFLOW
  Supervisor acknowledges    > status: pending
  Supervisor inspects        > status: assessment
  Supervisor approves        > status: pending_approval > assigned
                                       |                       |
  Technician needs parts   > status: awaiting_parts    > in_progress
  Part arrives             ^                           > testing
                                                       > completed
                                                       > returned_to_service

  BUS BACK IN SERVICE
  Bus status > active
  Driver notified: "Your bus is back in service"
  Maintenance record created as permanent log

-----------------------------------------------
7.4 PREVENTIVE MAINTENANCE FLOW
-----------------------------------------------

  Auto-generate creates schedules for every bus x every service type
             |
  Scheduler runs daily:
    - 7 days before due  > Warning notification (broadcast)
    - 3 days before due  > Alert notification (broadcast)
    - Past due date      > status: overdue
                         > bus locked (maintenance_locked = true)
                         > bus status: under_preventive_maintenance
             |
  Supervisor / Technician performs service > status: completed
             |
  System calculates next due date using bus priority score
  Bus unlocked > status: active

-----------------------------------------------
7.5 PRIORITY SCORING FOR PM INTERVALS
-----------------------------------------------

  SCORING FACTORS
  ---------------
  Factor                                              Points
  --------------------------------------------------  --------
  Vehicle age (4 pts/year, max 40)                    0 - 40
  Breakdowns in last 2 years (8 pts each, max 40)     0 - 40
  Maintenance records last 12 months (5 pts, max 20)  0 - 20
  Total mileage (1 pt per 6,250 km, max 20)           0 - 20

  INTERVAL APPLIED
  ----------------
  Score      Priority   Interval Used
  ---------  ---------  -------------------
  0 - 24     Low        100% of standard
  25 - 49    Medium     80% of standard
  50 - 79    High       65% of standard
  80 - 120   Critical   50% of standard

  Example: A bus scoring Critical gets a 90-day oil change shortened
  to 45 days.

===============================================
8. API DOCUMENTATION
===============================================

IOT SENSOR READINGS (ESP32 ENDPOINT)
--------------------------------------

  Endpoint:  POST /api/sensor-readings
  Header:    X-ESP32-Token: <your-esp32-secret>
  Content:   application/json

  Request Body:
  {
    "bus_id": 3,
    "temperature": 88.4,
    "vibration": 1.2,
    "oil_pressure": 45.0,
    "battery_voltage": 12.7
  }

  Response:
  {
    "status": "recorded",
    "health": "warning",
    "message": "Reading saved. Temperature is in warning range."
  }

  SENSOR THRESHOLDS
  -----------------
  Sensor                   Normal    Warning      Critical
  -----------------------  --------  -----------  --------
  Engine Temperature (C)   <= 85     85 - 95      > 95
  Vibration (g)            <= 1.5    1.5 - 2.5    > 2.5
  Oil Pressure (PSI)       >= 30     20 - 30      < 20
  Battery Voltage (V)      >= 12     11 - 12      < 11

  A reading is classified by its worst individual sensor.
  A Critical reading creates an immediate broadcast notification.

AI PREDICTION FEATURE SET
--------------------------

  Sent to Flask ML service at POST <FLASK_ML_URL>/predict

  Feature                   Description
  ------------------------  --------------------------------------------
  bus_mileage               Current odometer reading (km)
  days_since_last_service   Days since last maintenance record
  avg_temperature_30d       30-day rolling average temperature (C)
  avg_vibration_30d         30-day rolling average vibration (g)
  avg_pressure_30d          30-day rolling average oil pressure (PSI)
  failure_count_6m          Completed work orders in the past 6 months
  days_since_last_failure   Days since most recent completed work order
  service_interval_days     Standard PM interval for this bus

  Flask Response:
  {
    "risk_level": "high",
    "predicted_failure_type": "Engine Overheating",
    "confidence_score": 87.4,
    "recommended_action": "Schedule cooling system inspection within 3 days"
  }

===============================================
9. BUS STATUS REFERENCE
===============================================

  Status                          Meaning                               Dispatch?
  ------------------------------  ------------------------------------  ---------
  active                          At depot, in good condition, ready    YES
  on_trip                         Currently on the road with a driver   NO (in use)
  maintenance_due                 PM due within 7 days or overdue       WARNING
  under_preventive_maintenance    Locked for scheduled PM service       NO (locked)
  breakdown_reported              Driver submitted a breakdown report   NO
  under_repair                    Work order in progress                NO
  awaiting_spare_parts            Repair paused — part out of stock     NO
  ready_for_service               Repair done; awaiting sign-off        NO (pending)
  out_of_service                  Formally decommissioned               NO
  inactive                        Not in current use                    NO

  MAINTENANCE LOCK
  ----------------
  Independent of status, a bus can be maintenance-locked
  (maintenance_locked = true). When locked:
  - It cannot appear in the dispatch assignment form
  - A broadcast alert is sent to all staff
  - The lock releases automatically once all overdue PM is completed

===============================================
10. WORK ORDER STATUS REFERENCE
===============================================

  Status                What Is Happening                    Bus Status Impact
  --------------------  -----------------------------------  -----------------------
  reported              Fault logged, not yet reviewed       > breakdown_reported
  pending               Acknowledged, queued for inspection  —
  assessment            Bus being inspected                  —
  pending_approval      Awaiting management sign-off         —
  assigned              Technician assigned                  —
  awaiting_parts        Work paused, part out of stock       > awaiting_spare_parts
  in_progress           Technician actively repairing        > under_repair
  testing               Running road/engine tests            —
  completed             Tests passed, bus cleared            > ready_for_service
  returned_to_service   Supervisor confirmed, bus returned   > active
  cancelled             Work order voided                    —

  PRIORITY LEVELS
  ---------------
  Priority   Meaning
  ---------  -------------------------------------------------------
  Low        Minor cosmetic issue; bus can safely keep running
  Medium     Noticeable fault; address soon, not immediately dangerous
  High       Significant safety/performance fault; resolve within hours
  Critical   Bus unsafe or non-functional; immediate response required

